{
  "id": "pale-blue-dot",
  "title": "The Pale Blue Dot: Voyager's photo of Earth from 6 billion km",
  "voice": "af_heart",
  "speed": 1.0,
  "lead_in": 0.15,
  "tail": 0.9,
  "lines": [
    {"id": "L1",  "gap": 0.26, "text": "See that / tiny speck? / That's Earth, / and everyone / you've ever known."},
    {"id": "L2",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "Voyager {One|1} / snapped it / on February {fourteenth,|14,} / {nineteen ninety.|1990.}"},
    {"id": "L3",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "It was about / {six|6} billion kilometers / from the Sun."},
    {"id": "L4",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "Carl Sagan / first had / the idea / back in {nineteen eighty-one.|1981.}"},
    {"id": "L5",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "Voyager / turned around / and shot / {sixty|60} frames, / a family portrait / of our planets."},
    {"id": "L6",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "It caught / six planets. / Mars was lost / in sunlight, / and Mercury / sat too close / to the Sun."},
    {"id": "L7",  "gap": 0.34, "text": "And Earth? / Just {zero point one two|0.12} / of a single pixel."},
    {"id": "L8",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "That streak / across it? / A ray of sunlight / scattered / in the camera."},
    {"id": "L9",  "gap": 0.30, "text": "{Thirty-four|34} minutes later, / Voyager's cameras / were switched off."},
    {"id": "L10", "gap": 0.34, "text": "And the pictures / took until May / to make it home."},
    {"id": "L11", "gap": 0.0,  "text": "Follow for / part {four:|4:} / what happens / when Voyager's / power runs out."}
  ],
